In-Reply-To: <23hVnJDq8A8.wErhC7uypgsJ@ggplot2.groups.google.com>
References: <23hVnJDq8A8.wErhC7uypgsJ@ggplot2.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/ggplot2/c/23hVnJDq8A8/m/c2srjPaHdu4J>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

For Anyone who is interested (or who experiences this problem I found it was solved by simply using geom_map to plot the polygons, rather than geom_polygon. I have no idea why this would be so, but perhaps there is someone out there who could explain the theory behind how these two gems actually plot their data. So in the code in my previous post, instead of:

> geom_polygon(aes(long,lat,group=group))+

I used:

> geom_map(map=wa.gg <http://wa.gg>,aes(long,lat,map_id=id))+

Problem solved!

Cheers,

Simon

