When you set the axis limits to c(0.1,1) data values that represents the "bottom" of each bar falls outside those limits. The default action of ggplot for data that is outside those limits is to drop them completely. In the case of bars, this means you don't really have a bar to draw anymore. Try passing oob = rescale_none within scale_y_continuous. (oob stands for Out Of Bounds, I believe)

The behavior when the limits are set to c(-0.1,1.0) seems perfectly correct and natural to me. Was there something you thought was wrong with that version?

