Dear All,
Please find an easy snippet at the end of the email.
I am reusing some old code of mine and I noticed that now (on a fresh
ggplot2 installation from the R repositories on a box running Debian
mint), I am experiencing troubles.
When I run my snippet, I get this error message

source('test_ggplot2.R')
Error in structure(list(...), class = "options") :
   could not find function "unit"

The problem is given by the line

axis.ticks.length = unit(0.15, "cm")

inside ops(...). However, in the past on another machine, I have never got
any error message for this.
Is my new ggplot2 installation buggy or has anything changed recently in
its syntax?
In that case, what is the correct syntax now?
Many thanks for your help.
Cheers

Lorenzo

#################################################################

library(ggplot2)

mydata <- as.data.frame(cbind(seq(10), seq(10)))

names(mydata) <- c("ratio", "N")

b <- ggplot(mydata, aes(x=N, y=ratio))  +

  geom_point(size=2) +

   opts( panel.background=theme_rect(fill='white',
                    size=1.5))+
    opts(panel.grid.minor = theme_blank())+
    opts(panel.grid.major = theme_blank())+
       opts(axis.ticks = theme_segment(colour = "black", size=1)
            , axis.ticks.length = unit(0.15, "cm")
            )

pdf("test.pdf",width=5,height=5)

print(b)
dev.off()

