Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

I was playing and it looks like the problem is as.name <http://as.name>(). It puts single backwards quotes around the number which do not get parsed. When I took it out it seemed to work ok... check attachment.

>math_format
function (expr = 10^.x, format = force)
{
    quoted <- substitute(expr)
    subs <- function(x) {
        do.call("substitute", list(quoted, list(.x = as.name <http://as.name>(x))))
    }
    function(x) {
        x <- format(x)
        llply(x, subs)
    }
}
<environment: namespace:scales>

On Mon, Jun 25, 2012 at 2:26 PM, Thomas <thom...@gmail.com> wrote:
> p + scale_fill_gradient(trans='log10', guide=guide_colorbar(), breaks=trans_breaks('log10', function(x) 10^x), labels=trans_format('log10', math_format()))

